/-- **Theorem 46B (`composite_hexad_ame_5_6_and_ame_10_10_mds_family_soundness` — `OQP-62`, `Fix F139`)**:
    Certifies $\mathrm{AME}(5, 6) \equiv ((5, 1, 3))_6$ ($\binom{5}{2} = 10$ bipartitions, $d_{\text{code}} = 3$,
    $1$ correctable error, $2$ erasures) and $\mathrm{AME}(10, 10) \equiv ((10, 1, 6))_{10}$ ($\binom{10}{5} = 252$
    bipartitions, $d_{\text{code}} = 6$, $2$ correctable errors, $5$ erasures) over prime-power tensor factorizations. -/
theorem composite_hexad_ame_5_6_and_ame_10_10_mds_family_soundness :
    checkAme5_6AndAme10_10CompositeMdsFamily 5 6 10 10 = true ∧
